// TIME VORTEX — SPACE RAGA — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// TIME VORTEX as 60s psychedelic space raga — a game alternate of the Gravity Grid (gravity),
// selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Peter: "a bunch of remixes of cabinet songs that take advantage of the new guitar presets…
// a brand new remix for each cabinet theme… something different."
// 
// SPACE RAGA: "Within You Without You" and "Tomorrow Never Knows", Ravi Shankar by way of early
// Pink Floyd. A TANPURA drone on E and B never stops. The theme comes in on a SITAR, note for
// note on the theme's steps (TIME VORTEX's theremin line), with meend — slides, written as
// overlapping notes on the preset's legato glide — and gamak, fast slides round a held note. A
// 12-STRING chimes open-position arpeggios and strums (alternate-down, D··U D··U); a KOTO answers
// the sitar and doubles it in tremolo; a HARP sweeps every section end; a bowed STRING SECTION
// swells BACKWARDS (a 1.9 s linear attack cut dead on the downbeat), and a reversed cymbal leads
// into the changes. A tabla (song-local tuned drums: the dayan on E4, the bayan bending up) plays
// keherwa, tirakita fills and tihais, under a BASS that stays on the drone (E; B under the B7s).
// 
// THE HARMONY is the theme's, over the drone. Its A phrase is already a line cliché on an E pedal
// (Em · Em(maj7) · Em7 · A/E); its other chords become upper structures over E — Cmaj7/E,
// F♯m7♭5/E, G/E, D/E (the Dorian ♭VII), Am/E — and the B7s put the bass on B. The Fmaj7 bar
// (A5 F5 E5) is the Phrygian ♭II over E, resolved by the tune's own E5 on beat four; the bridge
// keeps its A♭ (E augmented over the pedal); the climax stays in E minor — a drone does not lift.
// Every part is voiced clear of the drone: no accompaniment C under C5 (it would rub the B2), no F
// under F5, no D♯ under D♯4; the 12-string's octave course is counted.
// 
//   1–4    tanpura, the sitar's alaap, koto drops, a harp sweep and a reversed swell (the cabinet screen loops it)
//   5–12   the theme on the sitar over tabla keherwa; koto answers; 12-string arpeggios and the bass from 9; tihai
//   13–20  the climb in upward meends; 12-string strum D··U D··U; backwards string swells every bar; tihai
//   21–28  the theme's second A as raga-rock: the 60s kit and tambourine join the tabla; picked 12-string
//   29–32  Tomorrow Never Knows: the sitar loop, the tom-led beat, the tabla in 3+3+2, Em ↔ D/E strums
//   33–36  the theme's Em · C · A♭ · B7: tabla and snare in gear shifts (6, 8, 12, 16), swells, koto tremolo
//   37–44  A2 with everything: strummed 12-string, chikari on the off-beats, harp arpeggios, koto
//   45–52  the B climb to F♯6, the 12-string doubling the sitar, chikari jhala in sixteenths, picked 12-string; tihai
//   53–56  the theme's wind-down; the kit out; a backwards swell into bar 5
//   57–60  past the loop (the jukebox ending): Em · C · A♭ · Em, a tihai to the last dha, the drone left ringing
// 
// Sounds: FRPP-6 sitar (frppSitar) on the theme, its chikari (Sitar · Chikari, song-local: poly, no
// glide); 12-string (frppTwelveString) picked through a slow phaser, strummed, and doubling the
// sitar in CLIMAX II; tanpura (frppTanpura); koto (frppKoto); harp (frppHarp); the bowed section on a
// reversed envelope (String section · Reversed, song-local); bass (frppBassNeck). The tabla is five
// song-local drum voices (Tabla · Na / Tin / Te / Ge / Ke); the kit is the Breakbeat kit with a
// tambourine; a song-local Reverse Cymbal. No CRLS-1 voice, no MRDR-3.
// 
// The mix is Peter's, from the desk (25 Oct): his master (an mbCompN preset and the limiter), the
// sitar's glide at 80 ms, the koto an octave down, his lane levels. Levelled on the trailing gain
// only: his −4 read −23.4 LUFS, -1.6 reads −21.0.
// 60 bars at 112, swing 54, 129 s; the loop 5–56 is 111 s; the cabinet screen loops 1–4.
// Written by work/local/_gravity-remix-space-raga.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs, which
// self-checks chord tones on the beats, off-chord notes as resolving approaches, semitone rubs
// against the drone, the bass and every sounding part (the 12-string's octave course counted), one
// note per string on the 12-string, the alternate strum's parity, every theme note on the sitar,
// the loop and cabinet-screen seams, and the cabinet's landmarks; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
